I think in reality the fix doesn't need to actually flush right? Right now it does things like
```
                _tos_cache1 = owner;
                _tos_cache0 = value;
                SET_CURRENT_CACHED_VALUES(2);
```
on an exit.
However, the fix could be just:
```
                SET_CURRENT_CACHED_VALUES(2);
```
right? Or am I misunderstanding? I know due to copy propagation, the compiler probably doesn't even emit the assigns. Which is why I'm approving it. It just makes the generated code read slightly worse.
